 ## Background
-The method originates from the ODC (Octree-based Discrete Curve) project by KAIST Visual AI Group [S1, unofficial]. It addresses the limitations of standard Marching Cubes in handling ambiguous cases, which can lead to topological errors. The QEF approach is inspired by the work on Quadric Error Metrics for mesh simplification [S2, unofficial], adapted here for vertex position optimization in surface extraction.
+The method originates from the ODC (Octree-based Direct Contouring) project by KAIST Visual AI Group [S1, unofficial]. It combines the structured grid traversal of Marching Cubes with the geometric optimization of QEF, a technique popularized by Garland and Heckbert for mesh simplification [S2, unofficial]. The QEM-based variant was proposed to address performance issues on parallel hardware [S2, unofficial].
 
